<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>11</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="LDPC_ScalingFactor" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>1.0</DataEntry>
<Description>scaling factor for input signal</Description>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>0</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="MCS" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>MCS</DataEntry>
<Description>modulation and coding scheme (MCS) for each user</Description>
<HideCondition>Payload_Config == 1</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="MCSTable" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>MCSTable</DataEntry>
<Description>The MCS index table to use for D-SCH, see section 5.1.3 and 6.1.4 of 38.214. [0: Table 5.1.3.1-1 | 1: Table 5.1.3.1-2 | 2: Table 5.1.3.1-3 | 3: Table 6.1.4.1-1 | 4: Table 6.1.4.1-2]</Description>
<HideCondition>Payload_Config == 1</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="MMSE_Config" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>0</DataEntry>
<Description>simplified mode estimates one SNR for MMSE channel estimation, but enhanced mode estimates SNR for each RBG received associated with one TX port and RX antenna. Besides, SpecifySNR allows user to specify SNR value.</Description>
<Enum>NR_PDSCH_ChannelEstimator__MMSE_Config@5G Advanced Modem Enums</Enum>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>16</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="MMSE_RBWinLen" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>1</DataEntry>
<Description>number of RBs for each MMSE-2D interpolation</Description>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>11</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="MaxHARQTrans" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>4</DataEntry>
<Description>maximum number of HARQ transmission per each HARQ process for each user</Description>
<HideCondition>HARQ_Enable == 0</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="Modulation" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>Modulation_t</DataEntry>
