terType;RRC_Alpha;SpecShapingScale;SaveVSASetupFile;VSASetupFile;AntennaPortIndex;Fill_OCNG</D></ParamOrder>
<Item XName="AntennaPortIndex" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>[0]</DataEntry>
<Description>PDSCH antenna port index used to be measured for each BWP</Description>
<HideCondition>SaveVSASetupFile==0</HideCondition>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="BWP_NumRBs" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>=BWP_NumRBs</DataEntry>
<Description>number of PRB in BWP basd on different SCS of different numerology</Description>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="BWP_RBOffset" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>=BWP_RBOffset</DataEntry>
<Description>the starting RB index of resource blocks allocated to BWP in the whole bandwidth based on SCS of 15KHz</Description>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="Bandwidth" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>Bandwidth</DataEntry>
<Description>bandwidth</Description>
<Enum>NR_VSA_Gen__BandWidth@5G Advanced Modem Enums</Enum>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>16</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="CI_StartPos" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>-3</DataEntry>
<Description>the start position of cyclic interval (without oversampling), compared to the start position of CP (negative means ahead of CP)</Description>
<HideCondition>1~=SpectrumShapingType</HideCondition>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>11</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="CORESET_Index" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>[1]</DataEntry>
<Description>a control resource set index in the range of 0 ~ 11, but 0 is not supported so far.</Description>
<HideCondition>PDCCH_Enable==0</HideCondition>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="CORESET_InterleaverSize" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>[6]</DataEntry>
<Description>the interleaver size (R) given by higher-layer parameter CORESET-interleaver-size. The value should be {2,3,6}</Description>
<HideCondition>PDCCH_Enable==0</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="CORESET_MappingType" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>[0]</DataEntry>
<Description>the CCE-to-REG mapping type for each CORESET in each BWP. 0 means non-interleaved while 1 means interleaved</Description>
<Enum />
<HideCondition>PDCCH_Enable==0</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="CORESET_NumSyms" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>[1]</DataEntry>
<Description>number of OFDM symbols in the time domain for each CORESET in each BWP. The value should be {1,2,3}</Description>
<HideCondition>PDCCH_Enable==0</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="CORESET_RB_Bitmap" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>[1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1]</DataEntry>
<Description>PRB bitmap for each CORESET in each BWP in ascending order. Each bit represents a non-overlapping group of 6 PRBs. LSB means the lowest group of 6 PRBs.</Description>
<HideCondition>PDCCH_Enable==0</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="CORESET_REG_BundleSize" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>[6]</DataEntry>
<Description>the REG bundle size for each CORESET in each BWP configured by the higher-layer parameter CORESET-REG-bundle-size. {2,6} for CORESET_NumSyms=1; {CORESET_NumSyms,6} for CORESET_NumSyms={2,3}</Description>
<HideCondition>PDCCH_Enable==0</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="CORESET_ShiftIndex" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>[0]</DataEntry>
<Description>the shift given by the higher-layer parameter CORESET-shift-index. The value should be {0,1,...,274}</Description>
<HideCondition>PDCCH_Enable==0</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="CORESET_SymOffset" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>[0]</DataEntry>
<Description>start OFDM symbol index in the time domain for each CORESET in each BWP.</Description>
<HideCondition>PDCCH_Enable==0</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="CSIRS_Density" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>1</DataEntry>
<Description>0: density = 0.5, 1: density = 1, 2: density = 3, density of CSI-RS transmission in frequency domain defined in Table 7.4.1.5.3-1: CSI-RS locations within a slot in 3GPP TS 38.211</Description>
<HideCondition>0==sum(CSIRS_Enable)</HideCondition>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="CSIRS_Enable" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>0</DataEntry>
<Description>0: disable CSI-RS, 1: enable NZP CSI-RS, 2: enable ZP CSI-RS</Description>
<Enum>NR_DL_MuxOFDMSym__CSIRS_Enable@5G Advanced Modem Enums</Enum>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="CSIRS_FirstSym" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>0</DataEntry>
<Description>the time-domain locations l0 in the range of {0, 1, ..., 13}</Description>
<HideCondition>0==sum(CSIRS_Enable)</HideCondition>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="CSIRS_FirstSym2" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>2</DataEntry>
<Description>the time-domain locations l1 in the range of {2, 3, ..., 12}, which is defined in section 7.4.1.5.3 in 3GPP TS 38.211</Description>
<HideCondition>0==sum(CSIRS_Enable)</HideCondition>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="CSIRS_FreqDomainBitmap" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>[1, 1, 1, 1]</DataEntry>
<Description>the bitmap is used to indicate CSI-RS symbols&apos; locations in frequency domain in each resource block (RB)</Description>
<HideCondition>0==sum(CSIRS_Enable)</HideCondition>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="CSIRS_N_ID" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>0</DataEntry>
<Description>N_ID for CSI-RS sequence generation</Description>
<HideCondition>0==sum(CSIRS_Enable)</HideCondition>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="CSIRS_NumRBs" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>20</DataEntry>
<Description>number of resource blocks (RBs) for each CSI-RS.</Description>
<HideCondition>0==sum(CSIRS_Enable)</HideCondition>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="CSIRS_Periodicity" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>4</DataEntry>
<Description>in the range of {4, 5, 8, 10, 16, 20, 32, 40, 64, 80, 160, 320, 640}, the periodicity (in slots) of CSI-RS transmission</Description>
<HideCondition>0==sum(CSIRS_Enable)</HideCondition>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="CSIRS_PosDot5" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>0</DataEntry>
<Description>0: Even, 1: Odd (CSI-RS could be transmitted in either even RBs or odd RBs when density=0.5)</Description>
<HideCondition>0==sum(CSIRS_Enable)</HideCondition>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="CSIRS_PowerBoosting" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>0</DataEntry>
<Description>CSI-RS power boosting in dB</Description>
<HideCondition>0==sum(CSIRS_Enable)</HideCondition>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>14</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="CSIRS_RBOffset" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>0</DataEntry>
<Description>the index of the first resource block (RB) allocated to each CSI-RS.</Description>
<HideCondition>0==sum(CSIRS_Enable)</HideCondition>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="CSIRS_RowIndexOfLocTable" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>1</DataEntry>
<Description>in the range of {1, 2, ..., 18}, the row index of Table 7.4.1.5.3-1: CSI-RS locations within a slot in 3GPP TS 38.211</Description>
<HideCondition>0==sum(CSIRS_Enable)</HideCondition>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="CSIRS_SlotOffset" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>0</DataEntry>
<Description>the slot offset (in slots) allocated to CSI-RS transmission in each CSI-RS transmission period.</Description>
<HideCondition>0==sum(CSIRS_Enable)</HideCondition>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="CellID" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>=CellID</DataEntry>
<Description>cell identity</Description>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>11</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="CyclicInterval" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>6</DataEntry>
<Description>the overlapped cyclic interval between two adjacent symbols in unit of chips (without oversampling), valid when SpectrumShapingType=TimeWindowing</Description>
<HideCondition>1~=SpectrumShapingType</HideCondition>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>11</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="CyclicPrefix" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>=CyclicPrefix</DataEntry>
<Description>normal CP or extended CP(0: Normal; 1: Extended)</Description>
<Enum />
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="DCI_BitNum" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>[20]</DataEntry>
<Description>the number of DCI bits for each PDCCH</Description>
<HideCondition>PDCCH_Enable==0</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="FCarrierTx" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>FCarrier</DataEntry>
<Description>frequency carrier of the transmitting signal</Description>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>0</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="FIR_FilterType" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>0</DataEntry>
<Description>spectrum-shaping FIR filter type, valid when SpectrumShapingType=FIRFilter</Description>
<Enum>NR_SpecShaping__FIR_FilterType@5G Advanced Modem Enums</Enum>
<HideCondition>2~=SpectrumShapingType</HideCondition>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>16</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="FIR_Taps" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>19</DataEntry>
<Description>number of FIR filter taps, valid when SpectrumShapingType=FIRFilter</Description>
<HideCondition>2~=SpectrumShapingType</HideCondition>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>11</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="Fill_OCNG" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>0</DataEntry>
<Description>Whether fill OCNG QPSK data for unused REs in Control Region and Data Region for FRC(Fixed Reference Channel)</Description>
<Enum>NR_DL_MuxOFDMSym__Fill_OCNG@5G Advanced Modem Enums</Enum>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>16</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="HARQ_Enable" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>0</DataEntry>
<Description>whether HARQ closed-loop transmission is enabled</Description>
<Enum>NR_HARQ_Controller__HARQ_Enable@5G Advanced Modem Enums</Enum>
<HideCondition>PDSCH_Enable ==0</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>16</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="LDPCBaseGraphType" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>=LDPCBaseGraphType</DataEntry>
<Description>LDPC base graph type. 0 : Base Graph1; 1 : Base Graph2;</Description>
<HideCondition>PDSCH_Enable==0||Payload_Config ==0</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="MCS" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>MCS</DataEntry>
<Description>modulation and coding scheme (MCS) for each user</Description>
<HideCondition>PDSCH_Enable==0||Payload_Config ==1</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="MCSTable" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>MCSTable</DataEntry>
<Description>The MCS index table. [0~2] for CP-OFDM. [1,3,4] for DFT-s-OFDM. [0: 64QAM table | 1: 256QAM table | 2: 64QAMLowSE table | 3: DFT-64QAM table | 4: DFT-64QAMLowSE]</Description>
<HideCondition>PDSCH_Enable==0||Payload_Config ==1</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="MaxHARQTrans" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>[4]</DataEntry>
<Description>maximum number of HARQ transmission per each HARQ process for each user</Description>
<HideCondition>PDSCH_Enable ==0||HARQ_Enable==0</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="Modulation" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>=Modulation_t</DataEntry>
<Description>the modulation orders in each slot. (1:QPSK, 2:16QAM, 3:64QAM, 4:256QAM).</Description>
<HideCondition>PDSCH_Enable==0||Payload_Config ==0</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="N_GridStart" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>[0]</DataEntry>
<Description>resource block start position according to point A for different BWP numerology</Description>
<Enum />
<HideCondition>ResourceGridEnable==0</HideCondition>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="NumBWPs" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>=NumBWPs</DataEntry>
<Description>number of BWPs</Description>
<Enum />
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Tunable><T>Bool</T><D>1</D></Tunable>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>11</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="NumHARQ" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>[8]</DataEntry>
<Description>number of HARQ processes for each user</Description>
<HideCondition>PDSCH_Enable ==0||HARQ_Enable==0</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="NumRFChains" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>=NumTxRFChains</DataEntry>
<Description>number of RF chain</Description>
<Enum />
<HideCondition>PortsRFMappingMode==0</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>11</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="Numerology" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>=Numerology</DataEntry>
<Description>numerology(0: 15kHz;1:30kHz;2:60kHz;3:120kHz;4:240kHz)</Description>
<Enum />
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="Numerology_k0" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>=Numerology_k0</DataEntry>
<Description>the lowest numbered subcarrier in a common resource block for unique BWP numerology</Description>
<Enum />
<HideCondition>ResourceGridEnable==1</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="OversamplingOption" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>=OversamplingOption</DataEntry>
<Description>oversampling  option</Description>
<Enum>FBMC_DemuxFrame__OversampleOption@5G Advanced Modem Enums</Enum>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Unit><T>Int</T><D>0</D></Unit>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>16</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="PBCH_DMRS_PowerBoosting" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>=PBCH_DMRS_PowerBoosting</DataEntry>
<Description>DMRS of PBCH power boosting in dB</Description>
<HideCondition>SSB_Enable ==0</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>0</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="PBCH_PowerBoosting" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>=PBCH_PowerBoosting</DataEntry>
<Description>PBCH power boosting in dB</Description>
<HideCondition>SSB_Enable ==0</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>0</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="PDCCH_AggregationLevel" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>[2]</DataEntry>
<Description>number of control-channel elements (CCEs) for each PDCCH in each BWP. The value should be {1, 2, 4, 8, 16}.</Description>
<HideCondition>PDCCH_Enable==0</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="PDCCH_AllocatedSlots" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>[0:9]</DataEntry>
<Description>Allocated slot indices for PDCCH in each frame for all BWPs. The index starts from 0 to (N-1), where N is the number of slots per frame.</Description>
<HideCondition>PDCCH_Enable==0</HideCondition>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="PDCCH_CandidateIndex" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>[0]</DataEntry>
<Description>PDCCH candidate index in the range of 0 ~ PDCCH_NumCandidates - 1.</Description>
<HideCondition>PDCCH_Enable==0</HideCondition>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="PDCCH_DMRS_MapMode" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>[1]</DataEntry>
<Description>PDCCH DMRS MapMode. 0: Map to CORESET; 1: Map to PDCCH only.</Description>
<HideCondition>PDCCH_Enable==0</HideCondition>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="PDCCH_DMRS_PowerBoosting" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>[0]</DataEntry>
<Description>DMRS power boosting in dB for each PDCCH.</Description>
<HideCondition>PDCCH_Enable==0</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>14</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="PDCCH_DMRS_ScramblingID" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>[0]</DataEntry>
<Description>PDCCH_DMRS_ScramblingID defined in 7.4.1.3.1/7.3.2.3 for each PDCCH in each BWP.</Description>
<HideCondition>PDCCH_Enable==0</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="PDCCH_Enable" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>0</DataEntry>
<Description>enable or disable PDCCH and its DMRS transmission</Description>
<Enum>NR_DL_MuxOFDMSym__PDCCH_Enable@5G Advanced Modem Enums</Enum>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>16</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="PDCCH_NumAllocatedSlots" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>[10]</DataEntry>
<Description>Number of allocated slots for PDCCH in each frame for each BWP.The size of this parameter is equal to NumBWPs</Description>
<HideCondition>PDCCH_Enable==0</HideCondition>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="PDCCH_NumCandidates" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>[4]</DataEntry>
<Description>number of PDCCH candidates. Allowed value are 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8.</Description>
<HideCondition>PDCCH_Enable==0</HideCondition>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="PDCCH_PowerBoosting" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>0.0</DataEntry>
<Description>power boosting in dB for each PDCCH</Description>
<HideCondition>PDCCH_Enable==0</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>14</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="PDCCH_n_RNTI" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>[1]</DataEntry>
<Description>the RNTI carried on CRC bits for PDCCH</Description>
<HideCondition>PDCCH_Enable==0</HideCondition>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="PDSCH_AllocatedSlots" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>ActiveSlots</DataEntry>
<Description>Allocated slot indices for PDSCH in each frame for all BWPs. The index starts from 0 to (N-1), where N is the number of slots per frame.</Description>
<HideCondition>PDSCH_Enable==0</HideCondition>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="PDSCH_DMRS_AddPos" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>=PDSCH_DMRS_AddPos</DataEntry>
<Description>DL-DMRSadd_pos. The number of additional positions for DMRS.</Description>
<HideCondition>PDSCH_Enable==0</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="PDSCH_DMRS_CDMGroupNum" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>PDSCH_DMRS_CDMGroupNum</DataEntry>
<Description>it&apos;s the number of CDM groups without data of values 1, 2, and 3, which refers to CDM groups {0}, {0, 1} and {0, 1, 2} respectively.</Description>
<HideCondition>PDSCH_Enable==0</HideCondition>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<Validate><T>Int</T><D>13</D></Validate></Item>
<Item XName="PDSCH_DMRS_ConfigType" Type="PartParam">
<DataEntry>=PDSCH_DMRS_ConfigType</DataEntry>
