<Item XName="Note" UserName="Note" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=DengXian&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=DengXian&gt;&amp;nbsp; &#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoTitle style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;NR DL Throughput&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Example&amp;nbsp;Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = &quot;o&quot; ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;This example showcases New Radio downlink system working in Frequency Range&amp;nbsp;1 (FR1) and Frequency Range (FR2). Upon the designs, throughput and BER can be measured.&amp;nbsp;Seven designs are in this workspace: SISO case, SISO BF case, MIMO 2x2 case, MIMO 2x2 BF case, SIMO switch diversity case,&amp;nbsp;SIMO&amp;nbsp;switch diversity BF&amp;nbsp;case, SISO HARQ case and MIMO 2x2 HARQ case. &lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Parameters FrequencyRange and Bandwidth is used in these examples and the realationship between bandwidth and number of RBs are shown in 38.104 table 5.3.2-1 and table 5.3.2-2, listed hereby in Appendix.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;SISO Case&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;In the SISO case, AWGN channel is used to help measure performance under different SNR values.&amp;nbsp;SystemConfiguraion specifies two types of NR signal configuration. One is FRC which are defined&amp;nbsp;by A.3.2 for FDD and A.3.3 for TDD&amp;nbsp;in 38.101-1 (V15.4.0). And the other is User Defined that user can configure the signal by specifying the parameters in the design SISO&apos;s Equation. The&amp;nbsp;settings used by this case is FRC defined in Table A.3.3.2.-1(Fixed Reference channel for receiver requirements (SCS 15kHz, TDD, QPSK 1/3)), and the&amp;nbsp;Bandwidth is 10MHz.&amp;nbsp;Switching to other FRC tables can be done by setting OperationMode and FRC_Table in the Equation.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;After the simulation, fractional throughput curve and uncoded BER curve are obtained. The simulated uncoded BER curve is compared with an ideal BER curve calculated by berawgn in MATLAB, where 0.1dB gap is observed. Please note that parameter &quot;MMSE_RBWinLen&quot; in the receiver would influence the performance in some degree. Run &lt;STRONG&gt;Sweep_SISO&lt;/STRONG&gt; equation to get the following curves:&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;1. Uncoded BER vs. SNR&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;2. Througput (%) vs. SNR&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;Note that in the SISO case, the sweep parameter in &lt;STRONG&gt;Sweep_SISO&lt;/STRONG&gt; equation&amp;nbsp;could be SNR or receiver power depending on the &lt;STRONG&gt;SweepMode&lt;/STRONG&gt; parameter. If &lt;STRONG&gt;SweepMode &lt;/STRONG&gt;is 0, SNR is swept and&amp;nbsp;receiver power is calculated with thermal noise of -174 dBm/Hz. If &lt;STRONG&gt;SweepMode &lt;/STRONG&gt;is 1, receiver power&amp;nbsp;is swept and&amp;nbsp;SNR is calculated with thermal noise of -174 dBm/Hz. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Calibri; FONT-WEIGHT: normal; FONT-STYLE: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Note that if RF models in the design have noise figure (NF), set NF value accordingly in the equation to get expect results (i.e. calculated receiver power for &lt;STRONG&gt;SweepMode&lt;/STRONG&gt; &lt;STRONG&gt;0 &lt;/STRONG&gt;or SNR for &lt;STRONG&gt;SweepMode 1&lt;/STRONG&gt;).&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Calibri; FONT-WEIGHT: normal; FONT-STYLE: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Calibri; FONT-WEIGHT: normal; FONT-STYLE: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;SISO BF Case&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;In the SISO BF Case, beamforming architecture is introduced. Both TX and RX do beam training at the same time.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;After the beam training, PDSCH transmission starts based on the optimal TX and RX beam.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;Some notes related to current design:&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;OL style=&quot;MARGIN-TOP: 0in&quot; type=1&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;PDSCH associated with port 1000 are transmitted in TX side and received in RX side to measure the performance.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;SSB associated with port 4000 is used to do beam training for both of TX side and RX side.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Two TX RF chains and three RX RF chains are deployed. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Port 1000 is associated with PDSCH transmission and port 4000 is associated with SSB transmission. PortRFMappingMatrix defines the mapping relationship between ports and TX RF chains. For example, PortRFMappingMatrix = [1;0;0;1] is the vectorization of the mapping matrix with dimension NumOfTxRFChains-by-NumOfPorts, which indicates PDSCH in port 1000 are mapped to TX RF chain #0 and SSB in port 4000 is mapped to TX RF chain #1.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;SSB number, SSB_Lmax in the example&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&#x2019;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;s Parameters List, determines the maximum available TX beams&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&#x2019;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt; number, which is 4 in this example. The beam direction of each SSB is specified by TxThetaTable([90;90;90;90]) and TxPhiTable([60;20;340;300]) in the Equations of design.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;DataRcvRxRFChainsList and BeamTrainingRxRFChainsList are introduced in the RX side to indicate the usage of RX RF chains. For example, in current design, NumRxRFChains = 3, DataRcvRxRFChainsList = [0] and BeamTrainingRxRFChainsList = [1;2] indicate the RX RF chain #0 to receive PDSCH and RX RF chains #1 and #2 to receive SSB to perform beam training.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;NumberBeamTrainingRounds and the number of RX RF chains associated with beam training (=length(BeamTrainingRxRFChainsList)) together determine the number of&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;maximum available RX beams which equals to NumberBeamTrainingRounds&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;multiplying the number of RX RF chains associated with beam training. In current design, NumberBeamTrainingRounds =&amp;nbsp;2 and two RX RF chains for beam training imply&amp;nbsp;4 available RX beams. The beam direction of RX beams are specified by RxThetaTable([90;90;90;90]) and RxPhiTable([60;20;340;300]) in the Equations of design.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;NumTxAnts and NumRxAnts specify the real phase array topology.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;A 3D channel model is used to model a LOS channel, whose ClusterAoD = 340 and ClusterAoA = 20. Therefore, the optimal TX beam is the 3&lt;SUP&gt;rd&lt;/SUP&gt; one, and the optimal RX beam is the 2&lt;SUP&gt;nd&lt;/SUP&gt; one.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/OL&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;MIMO 2X2 Case&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;In the MIMO case, 2X2 SU MIMO is simulated with 3D channel model to emulate the MIMO channel, where UMi is used as default. For MIMO case, there is no benchmark for BER vs. SNR.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 9pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;MIMO 2x2 &lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;BF Case&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;In the&amp;nbsp;MIMO BF Case, beamforming architecture is introduced. Both TX and RX do beam training at the same time. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;After the beam training, PDSCH transmission starts based on the optimal TX and RX beam.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;Some notes relate to MIMO BF design, only aspects different from SISO BF Case are elaborated hereby:&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;OL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;PDSCH associated with port 1000 and port 1001 are transmitted in TX side and received in RX side to measure the performance&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Three TX RF chains and four RX RF chains are deployed. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Upon the configuration of PortRFMappingMatrix = [1;0;0;0;1;0;0;0;1] BeamTrainingRxRFChainsList = [2;3] and DataRcvRxRFChainsList = [0;1]. In&amp;nbsp;both TX side and RX side, the first and second RF chains are used to transmit data.&amp;nbsp;In TX side, the third RF chain is used to do beam training. In the RX side, the third and the fourth RF chains are used to do beam training.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;For demo purpose, four avaliable TX beams and four avaliable&amp;nbsp;RX beams are included in the simulation, say TxThetaTable = [90;90;90;90]/180*pi; TxPhiTable = [60;20;340;300]/180*pi; RxThetaTable = [90;90;90;90]/180*pi; RxPhiTable = [60;20;340;300]/180*pi;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Accordingly, ChTxTheta = TxThetaTable([2,4])/pi*180; ChTxPhi = TxPhiTable([2,4])/pi*180; ChRxTheta = RxThetaTable([1,3])/pi*180; and ChRxPhi = RxPhiTable([1,3])/pi*180; are configured for channel modeling to accommodate two layer transmission.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/OL&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;SIMO Switch Diversity Case&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;In the SIMO case, a parameter &quot;DiversityOption&quot; is added to the receiver to specify if diversity takes effect:&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;1. If DiversityOption=0, the diversity would be enabled, where the branch with higher power would be picked for demodulation and decoding.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;2. If DiversityOption=1, only the first branch takes effect.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;3. If DiversityOption=2, only the second branch takes effect.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;In the SIMO diversity case, two branches in RX side are deployed to dynamically switch the effective receiving path upon power estimation.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;SIMO Switch&amp;nbsp;Diversity BF Case&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;Beamforming procedure is added to the conventional diversity case. In this case, only one stream in each diversity branch is supported. In the receiver side, one diversity branch is selected from the two diversity branches upon a simple metric which compares DMRS power in both diversity branches.&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;SISO&amp;nbsp;HARQ Case&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=DengXian&gt;In&amp;nbsp;SISO HARQ case, NR downlink closed-loop HARQ is supported&amp;nbsp;to measure Throughput under&amp;nbsp;different SNR in&amp;nbsp;AWGN channel.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=DengXian&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;Four typical FRC&amp;nbsp;(Fixed Referenced Channel) are available&amp;nbsp;in this example, two for FDD&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;the other two&amp;nbsp;for TDD according to&amp;nbsp;Table A.3.2.2-1,&amp;nbsp;A.3.2.2-2&amp;nbsp;and A.3.3.2-1,&amp;nbsp;A.3.3.2-2&amp;nbsp;in 38.101-1 (V15.5.0).&amp;nbsp;Different &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;FRC table can configured&amp;nbsp;through&amp;nbsp;variable FRC_Config in&amp;nbsp;Equation. Default bandwidth&amp;nbsp;in this case&amp;nbsp;is 10MHz, which is also configurable. When simulation is over&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;, fractional throughput curve is&amp;nbsp;plotted on&amp;nbsp;figures.&amp;nbsp;Running &lt;STRONG&gt;Sweep_SISO_AWGN_HARQ&lt;/STRONG&gt; equation to get the following curves:&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=DengXian&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;1. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;Througput (%) vs. SNR&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=DengXian&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Calibri; FONT-WEIGHT: normal; FONT-STYLE: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Calibri; FONT-WEIGHT: normal; FONT-STYLE: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=DengXian&gt;The following&amp;nbsp;settings and instructions should be paid attention to in order&amp;nbsp;to support&amp;nbsp;HARQ simulation:&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;OL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=DengXian&gt;Set&amp;nbsp;appropriate&amp;nbsp;synchronization&amp;nbsp;settings&amp;nbsp;for&amp;nbsp;NR_DL_Numerology_Rcv. One way to&amp;nbsp;support HARQ simulation is setting&amp;nbsp;&apos;AutoFrameSync&apos;&amp;nbsp;as NO, which&amp;nbsp;then requires manual setup of time and frequency synchronization offset&amp;nbsp;to&amp;nbsp;the received signal through &apos;DesiredDelay&apos; and &apos;DesiredFreqOffset&apos;. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=DengXian&gt;For AWGN channel, &apos;DesiredDelay&apos; will usually be&amp;nbsp;0&amp;nbsp;if no additional&amp;nbsp;time delay is introduced in simulation link.&amp;nbsp;For other multipath channels, however, it is&amp;nbsp;recommended to observe the auto-detected result from&amp;nbsp;TO&amp;nbsp;output of NR_DL_Numerology_Rcv by&amp;nbsp;setting&amp;nbsp;&apos;AutoFrameSync&apos;&amp;nbsp;to YES and&amp;nbsp;&apos;HARQ_Enable&apos; to NO.&amp;nbsp;Using the auto-detected TO&amp;nbsp;result to configure&amp;nbsp;&apos;DesiredDelay&apos;.&amp;nbsp;&apos;DesiredFreqOffset&apos;&amp;nbsp;is&amp;nbsp;set to 0 if there is no additional frequency offset in&amp;nbsp;simulation link.&amp;nbsp;Another&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=DengXian&gt; way to&amp;nbsp;support HARQ simulation is&amp;nbsp;setting &apos;AutoFrameSync&apos; to YES while selecting&amp;nbsp;&apos;CP+DMRS Synchronization&apos; for&amp;nbsp;&apos;SyncMethod&apos;.&amp;nbsp;This way, receiver will&amp;nbsp;perform&amp;nbsp;automatic frame synchronization by using cyclic prefix&amp;nbsp;and DMRS&amp;nbsp;of the received signal.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=DengXian&gt;Set&amp;nbsp;&apos;HARQ_Enable&apos; parameter in both NR top-level source and receiver. In this example, users can just set the HARQ_Enable in the Parameters Tab.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=DengXian&gt;Set&amp;nbsp;&apos;NumHARQ&apos; parameter to specify the number of HARQ processes.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=DengXian&gt;Set&amp;nbsp;&apos;MaxHARQTrans&apos; parameter to specify maximum number of HARQ transmission; The &apos;RV_Sequence&apos; parameter specifies the redundancy version coding sequence. Its&amp;nbsp;array size should be equal to that of&amp;nbsp;&apos;MaxHARQTrans&apos; parameter.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=DengXian&gt;In&amp;nbsp;HARQ simulation, output delay in NR top-level receiver&amp;nbsp;is&amp;nbsp;one slot (1ms for Numerology 0 and 0.5ms for other Numerology setting). &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT face=DengXian&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;As HARQ is&amp;nbsp;not supported&amp;nbsp;by setting YES for &apos;AutoFrameSync&apos;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&apos;SSB Synchronization&apos; for &apos;SyncMethod&apos;, MaxSSBIndex and SSBPower outputs &lt;/SPAN&gt;are invalid&amp;nbsp;and shown&amp;nbsp;as -999. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=DengXian&gt;When &apos;AutoFrameSync&apos; is set to YES and &apos;SyncMethod&apos; is set to &apos;SSB Synchronization&apos;, which is&amp;nbsp;only valid&amp;nbsp;for non-HARQ case,&amp;nbsp;NR top-level receiver output&amp;nbsp;delay is SSB_Periodicity*NumBeamTrainingRounds.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=DengXian&gt;Connection of&amp;nbsp;output port &apos;HARQ_Bits&apos; of&amp;nbsp;NR_DL_Numerology_Rcv&amp;nbsp;with&amp;nbsp;input port &apos;HARQ_Bits&apos;&amp;nbsp;of&amp;nbsp;NR_DL_Source.&amp;nbsp;A Delay&amp;nbsp;value of&amp;nbsp;(NumHARQ-HarqRxDelay) is required&amp;nbsp;between these two ports to support HARQ simulation. For Numerology 0 and 1, HarqRxDelay is 1 since delay of output from&amp;nbsp;receiver&amp;nbsp;is&amp;nbsp;one time slot for HARQ simulation where&amp;nbsp;CP+DMRS Synchronization or AutoFrameSync OFF is adopted. While&amp;nbsp;for Numerology 2&amp;nbsp;and 3, as the minimum output delay of the receiver is 0.5ms, which corresponds to 2 time slots for Numerology 2 and 4 time slots for Numerology 3, HarqRxDelay therefore should be 2 and&amp;nbsp;4 for SCS 60kHz and 120kHz setting. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=DengXian&gt;&lt;EM&gt;Note&amp;nbsp;that &lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;HARQ is&amp;nbsp;not&amp;nbsp;supported by Numerology 4. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=DengXian&gt;FIR Filter in the top-level source will introduce additional&amp;nbsp;reception delay. Hence, SpectrumShapingType is highly recommended to be 0 for HARQ simulation.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/OL&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=DengXian&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;MIMO&amp;nbsp;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;2x2 &lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;HARQ Case&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: left; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=left&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=DengXian&gt;In the MIMO&amp;nbsp;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;HARQ case, 2X2 SU MIMO is simulated with 3D channel model to emulate the MIMO channel, where CDL-A is used as default.&amp;nbsp;The same&amp;nbsp;as SISO HARQ case, f&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=DengXian&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;our typical FRC settings are used in this example&amp;nbsp;according to&amp;nbsp;Table A.3.2.2-1,&amp;nbsp;A.3.2.2-2&amp;nbsp;for FDD and A.3.3.2-1,&amp;nbsp;A.3.3.2-2&amp;nbsp;for TDD in 38.101-1 (V15.5.0). &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;FRC tables can be selected&amp;nbsp;by setting FRC_Config in the Equation. Default bandwidth&amp;nbsp;in this case&amp;nbsp;is 10MHz, which is also configurable&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;.&amp;nbsp;When&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;simulation is over, fractional throughput curve is&amp;nbsp;plotted on&amp;nbsp;figures. Running &lt;STRONG&gt;Sweep_MIMO_HARQ&lt;/STRONG&gt; equation to get the following curves:&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=DengXian&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;1. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;Througput (%) vs. SNR&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=DengXian&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=DengXian&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=DengXian&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Signal Power Setting&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;In each design, there is one or several Oscillators following the NR_DL_Source. The Oscillator is used to tune the signal power to a specific power level, together with NR_DL_Source.&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;If there&amp;nbsp;are one port and one RF chain for the signal transmission, the signal power setting is straightforward:&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;If you specify the Power Parameter to, say 20, in Oscillator with unit dBm, the signal would be tuned to be with power 20dBm/15kHz in the frequency range where it&apos;s allocated.&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;No matter what subcarrier spacing is used, the power spectrum would be 20dBm/15kHz in the frequency range where it&apos;s allocated.&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;That means if 30kHz subcarrier spacing is specified, it results in 23dBm/30kHz.&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;Normally, multiple ports would be configured. Therefore the resulting signal power spectrum&amp;nbsp;would vary upon different configurations.&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;Let&apos;s assume Power is still set to 20. and Let&apos;s&amp;nbsp;take an&amp;nbsp;example: if three ports are configured: port 1000 and port&amp;nbsp;1001 for PDSCH transmission and port&amp;nbsp;4000 for SSB transmission. Three RF chains are equipped for the transmission.&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;If PortRFMappingMatrix = [1 0 0 1 1 1], the first RF chain transmit both port 1000 signal and port 4000 signal. Considering port 4000 signal is only transmitted in limited slots, the power spectrum would be still 20dBm/15kHz in the frequence range where PDSCH is allocated. The same thing happens for the second RF chain.&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;If PortRFMappingMatrix = [1 1 1 1 1 1], which means signals associated with port 1000, port 1001 and port 4000 are all transmitted in both RF chains. In this case, the power spectrum would be 23dBm/15kHz in the frequency range where PDSCH transmission is allocated.&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;The setting PortRFMappingMatrix = [1 1 1 1 1 1] doesn&apos;t make sense if you want to succeed the transmission, but it&apos;s a good example to elaborate the power setting hereby.&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Appendix&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 14pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: DengXian&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&g